# policy texts used in round 3:
## careful: Safety first. Above 30 m, fall no faster than 3 m/s; below 30 m, no faster than 1.5 m/s. While the pad is still more than 20 m to the side, do not descend below 40 m: hold height and move toward the pad. Move sideways only slowly and stop drifting once over the pad. Touch down very gently and upright. Use fuel freely if it keeps the ship safe.
## fuel-miser: Conserve fuel above all. Let gravity do the work: above 25 m, falling up to 6 m/s is fine and the engine should stay off. Below 25 m, brake just enough to fall no faster than 3 m/s at touchdown. Drift toward the pad without wasting fuel and stop drifting once over it. Land upright on the pad.
## aggressive: Land as quickly as possible. Above 30 m, fall fast, up to 8 m/s. Below 30 m, brake hard to fall no faster than 3.5 m/s at touchdown. Move quickly toward the pad, then stop drifting once over it. Never climb. A hard but survivable touchdown on the pad, upright, is fine.
